    "Possessing the right asset class is only half the battle; to succeed over decades, you must execute the right investment methodology. The primary reason amateur retail investors lose money in the stock market is not because the stock market is flawed, but because Human Psychology Is Flawed. When the market is booming and stock prices are at all-time highs, retail investors feel intense greed and FOMO (fear of missing out), pouring their life savings into equities at the top.",
    "Conversely, when economic recessions strike and stock markets crash by thirty or forty percent, headlines scream panic, and retail investors succumb to acute terror. They sell their holdings at the very bottom, locking in catastrophic losses, and vow never to invest in the stock market again. They buy high out of greed, and sell low out of fear?the exact mathematical recipe for poverty.",
    "To eliminate destructive human emotion and guarantee superior long-term returns, you must deploy Dollar-Cost Averaging (DCA). Dollar-cost averaging is the systematic discipline of investing a Fixed Dollar Amount into a broad-market asset on a Fixed Calendar Schedule (e.g., $100 every single Monday morning), Regardless of Market Conditions.",
    "Notice the radical simplicity and power of this system: You do not look at stock charts, you do not listen to market analysts on television, and you do not care whether the stock market is at an all-time high or in the depths of a brutal bear market. On Monday morning, your automated transfer executes, and one hundred dollars of broad-market index fund shares are purchased with robotic precision.",
    "The mathematical elegance of dollar-cost averaging lies in how it automatically capitalizes on market fluctuations through Geometric Share Accumulation. When stock prices are high, your one hundred dollars automatically buys fewer shares. When stock prices crash by forty percent during a recession, your one hundred dollars automatically buys significantly more shares at a steep discount.",
    "Consider the psychological inversion this creates. A dollar-cost averaging investor does not fear market crashes; They Celebrate Market Crashes. A market crash is not a tragedy; it is a Generational 40% Off Sale on the greatest companies on earth. When the stock market crashes, your automated weekly contributions are accumulating shares at bargain-basement prices.",
